    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d245">

                <pb facs="0458" n="1526" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v05p2/pg1526"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.5/12–2754</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Foreign Secretary Eden
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d245-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1954-12-27">December 27,
                        1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Anthony</hi>:] Thanks for your message.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d245-f2"/> I have been thinking along the same lines. It looks
                    at the moment I dictate this as though the treaties would squeak through, but I
                    suppose we shall not know definitely for a couple of days. In the meantime, we
                    should be ready. The President is in Augusta and would immediately return here
                    if the vote goes wrong. I have talked with him by phone and he agrees in
                    principle that there must be quick action. I would be prepared, as you suggest,
                    to come to Europe, and in general my ideas harmonize with yours. While I would
                    enjoy seeing you again, I hope it will not be necessary on this occasion.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Foster Dulles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d245-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d245-f1-content">
                <p>This message was transmitted to the Embassy in London in telegram 3377, Dec. 27,
                    with the request that the Ambassador personally deliver it to Eden.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d245-f2" n="2" xml:id="d245-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
